Data:
1	"GOLD"	"Gold"	"Gold %gold_icon% is the primary currency in the world. It is earned through trade, production, and political influence. Managing your gold wisely is key to building a dynasty.%n%%n%Your treasury currently holds %gold% %gold_icon%."	""	""	|
2	"FAME"	"Fame"	"Fame represents your family's renown across the land. Higher fame unlocks access to greater political offices and social standing.%n%%n%The dynasty %my_crest% %dyn_color%%dyn_surname%%color_reset% has %fame% fame and %imperial_fame% imperial fame."	""	""	|
3	"FAVOR"	"Favor"	"Favor reflects how much a character likes or trusts another. High favor opens doors to alliances, marriages, and political support."	""	""	|
4	"PATRON_GUILD"	"Patron Guild"	"The guild of merchants and traders. Patrons deal in goods, run markets, and control trade routes."	"hud/guide/patron.tga"	""	|
5	"ARTISAN_GUILD"	"Artisan Guild"	"The guild of craftsmen. Artisans produce weapons, tools, and refined goods."	"hud/guide/artisan.tga"	""	|
6	"SCHOLAR_GUILD"	"Scholar Guild"	"The guild of scholars and healers. Scholars run churches, hospitals, and alchemist shops."	"hud/guide/scholar.tga"	""	|
7	"ROGUE_GUILD"	"Rogue Guild"	"The guild of rogues and thieves. Rogues operate taverns, robber camps, and shady dealings."	"hud/guide/rogue.tga"	""	|
8	"ALDERMAN"	"Alderman"	"The Alderman is the senior figure of the guild house, and usually excels at what they do. They can impose economic measures on the town.%n%%n%Current Alderman of %settlement%:%n%%officer_color:alderman%%officer:alderman%%color_reset%."	""	"alderman"	|
9	"GUILD_MASTER"	"Guild Master"	"A Guild Master leads one of the four guilds (Patron, Artisan, Scholar, Rogue)."	""	""	|
10	"NOBILITY"	"Nobility Title"	"Your nobility title determines your social rank. Higher titles grant access to more powerful offices and larger estates.%n%%n%Your current title: %my_crest% %dyn_color%%nobility%%color_reset%."	""	""	|
11	"OFFICE"	"Political Office"	"Offices are positions of power in settlements. Holding an office grants income, privileges, and influence over the town."	""	""	|
12	"DYNASTY"	"Dynasty"	"Your dynasty is your family line. Everything you build, from wealth to political power, passes down through generations.%n%%n%You lead the %my_crest% %dyn_color%%dyn_surname%%color_reset% dynasty, playing as %char_name%."	""	"player"	|
13	"SETTLEMENT"	"Settlement"	"Settlements are the towns and cities where commerce and politics take place.%n%%n%You are currently in %settlement% (a %settlement_tier_name%, level %settlement_level%)."	""	""	|
14	"COURT"	"The Court"	"The court is where justice is served. Characters can bring accusations, present evidence, and influence the jury to punish rivals.%n%%n%Current severity of law in %settlement%: %severity_of_law_name%."	""	""	|
15	"EVIDENCE"	"Evidence"	"Evidence is gathered through espionage and observation. Presenting strong evidence in court increases your chance of a guilty verdict."	""	""	|
16	"MEASURE"	"Measures"	"Measures are actions your characters can take, from trading goods to filing lawsuits. Each measure costs time and sometimes money."	""	""	|
17	"EXPERIENCE"	"Experience"	"Characters gain experience %xp_icon% through work and combat. Higher experience improves skills and unlocks new abilities.%n%%n%%char_name% is level %level_icon% with %xp% %xp_icon%."	""	""	|
18	"HITPOINTS"	"Hit Points"	"Hit points %hp_icon% represent a character's health. When they reach zero, the character dies. Rest and healing restore hit points.%n%%n%%char_name%: %hp_cur% / %hp_max% %hp_icon%."	""	""	|
